drm/sun4i: de33: CTM property on the VI planes

Adds a "CTM" blob property to every DE33 VI plane: 12 u64, row-major
[A | b], each S31.32 sign-magnitude (the layout of upstream's
drm_color_ctm_3x4, which 6.18 carries only in amdgpu_drm.h), on RGB
normalised to [0,1], applied after the plane's YUV->RGB conversion.
The driver folds it into the channel's CCSC: C' = A.C, and the offset
b goes into the luma pre-offset (the post-constants cannot carry a
negative offset on this hardware), which holds it exactly when it is a
grey shift along C'[.][Y] -- the shape of a colour grade's lift. The
correction costs nothing at scanout. Unset (or blob 0) leaves the stock
table bit for bit: the identity CTM composes to exactly the
BT.709-limited table. A CTM that does not fit -- a combined coefficient
of 4.0 or more (the field is signed 20-bit and wraps), an offset that is
not a grey shift, a pre-offset out of its field -- fails atomic_check
with -ERANGE. RGB framebuffers (CSC off) ignore it; UI planes and
DE2/DE3 mixers do not get it.

mabur uses it to undo the drone's ColorTrans sensor tuning on the
video plane only, leaving the OSD plane alone. Register limits were
measured on an H618: mabur docs/findings/2026-10-12-opi-colortrans-probe.md.
Superseded by the colour pipeline API (colorop CTM_3X4) on a kernel that
has it.

